{% comment %}
  Review highlights: a few good reviews in a bordered box, one at a time, for beside the
  Add to cart button.

  The review list sits far down a product page, below the description, and most shoppers
  decide before they get there. This puts a handful of reviews where the decision is made:
  the merchant's featured ones, a random few, or the latest, each with the reviewer's
  initial, name, a "Verified" pill for a review tied to a real order, the stars and the
  start of the text.

  Design constraints, shared with the review block for the same reasons:

  - **Deferred load.** Fetched when the block nears the viewport. Beside Add to cart that is
    usually at once, but the script still waits on a long page rather than assuming.
  - **No layout shift.** The box is drawn here with placeholders at its final height, and
    it never changes height as it rotates: every review's text is held to the same number
    of lines. Content below it, often the Add to cart button itself, never moves under the
    shopper's finger. With nothing to show it is removed and takes no space.
  - **Nothing invented.** "Verified" only for a review the app matched to an order, the
    incentive disclosure on every review written under an offer (FTC 16 CFR 465), and
    only published reviews, which is all the endpoint returns.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign lines = block.settings.lines | default: 4

  comment
    The colours are per placement and optional: blank follows the colours set in the app
    (Settings -> Display), the same as the review cards. A background picked here gets a
    text colour paired to it by the script, so a dark box never meets dark theme text.
  endcomment
  assign style = '--rm-hl-lines:' | append: lines | append: ';'
  if block.settings.border_color != blank
    assign style = style | append: '--rm-hl-border:' | append: block.settings.border_color | append: ';'
  endif
  if block.settings.background_color != blank
    assign style = style | append: '--rm-hl-bg:' | append: block.settings.background_color | append: ';'
  endif

  comment
    Which of the merchant's widgets lends this box its look (star shape, colours, font),
    from the page it is on. The review block asks the merchant; this block has nothing else
    to say about placement, so it works it out rather than adding a setting.
  endcomment
  case request.page_type
    when 'product'
      assign placement = 'product_page'
    when 'collection'
      assign placement = 'collection_page'
    when 'index'
      assign placement = 'home_page'
    else
      assign placement = ''
  endcase
-%}

<div
  class="rm-hl"
  data-rm-highlights
  data-rm-shop="{{ shop.permanent_domain }}"
  data-rm-product="{{ product.id }}"
  data-rm-placement="{{ placement }}"
  data-rm-app-url="{{ block.settings.app_url | default: 'https://reviewmaster-app.azurewebsites.net' | escape }}"
  data-rm-source="{{ block.settings.source }}"
  data-rm-limit="{{ block.settings.count }}"
  data-rm-rotate="{{ block.settings.rotate_seconds }}"
  data-rm-show-stars="{{ block.settings.show_stars }}"
  data-rm-show-badge="{{ block.settings.show_verified }}"
  data-rm-show-avatar="{{ block.settings.show_avatar }}"
  data-rm-design-mode="{{ request.design_mode }}"
  {% if block.settings.background_color != blank %}data-rm-hl-bg="{{ block.settings.background_color | color_to_hex }}"{% endif %}
  {% comment %}
    The box's words in the shopper's language, read by the script (readLocale). escape_once,
    because `t` already escapes and a second escape would show "&amp;" on the page.
  {% endcomment %}
  data-rm-t-read-more="{{ 'reviewmaster.read_more' | t | escape_once }}"
  data-rm-t-show-less="{{ 'reviewmaster.show_less' | t | escape_once }}"
  data-rm-t-verified-short="{{ 'reviewmaster.verified_short' | t | escape_once }}"
  data-rm-t-about-product="{{ 'reviewmaster.about_product' | t | escape_once }}"
  data-rm-t-highlights-empty="{{ 'reviewmaster.highlights_empty' | t | escape_once }}"
  data-rm-t-highlights-label="{{ 'reviewmaster.highlights_label' | t | escape_once }}"
  data-rm-t-previous-review="{{ 'reviewmaster.previous_review' | t | escape_once }}"
  data-rm-t-next-review="{{ 'reviewmaster.next_review' | t | escape_once }}"
  data-rm-t-slide-label="{{ 'reviewmaster.slide_label' | t | escape_once }}"
  data-rm-t-pause-rotation="{{ 'reviewmaster.pause_rotation' | t | escape_once }}"
  data-rm-t-play-rotation="{{ 'reviewmaster.play_rotation' | t | escape_once }}"
  style="{{ style }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    Placeholders in the same structure as a real review, so the box is drawn at its final
    height before anything is fetched and the script swaps content without moving the page.
    No more placeholder lines than text lines, or a two-line box would load taller than it
    ends up. Decorative, so hidden from assistive tech.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign skel_lines = lines | at_most: 3 -%}
  <div class="rm-hl__slides" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="rm-hl__slide">
      <div class="rm-hl__head">
        {%- if block.settings.show_avatar -%}<span class="rm-hl__avatar rm-hl__avatar--skel"></span>{%- endif -%}
        <div class="rm-hl__who">
          <span class="rm-skel rm-skel--line rm-skel--short"></span>
          {%- if block.settings.show_stars -%}<span class="rm-skel rm-skel--stars"></span>{%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rm-hl__quote">
        {%- for i in (1..skel_lines) -%}
          <span class="rm-skel rm-skel--line{% if forloop.last %} rm-skel--short{% endif %}"></span>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="rm-hl__foot"></div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  No manual <script> tag: declaring "javascript" in the schema makes Shopify serve the
  asset from its CDN, deduplicated across blocks, so a page with this box and the review
  list loads reviewmaster.js once.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Review highlights",
  "target": "section",
  "stylesheet": "reviewmaster.css",
  "javascript": "reviewmaster.js",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "source",
      "label": "Which reviews",
      "default": "featured",
      "options": [
        { "value": "featured", "label": "Featured" },
        { "value": "random", "label": "Random" },
        { "value": "latest", "label": "Latest" }
      ],
      "info": "Featured = reviews you mark with Feature in Marka Reviews → All reviews. When there are not enough, recent 4 and 5 star reviews fill the rest. Random and Latest use 4 and 5 star reviews with some text."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "count",
      "label": "Number of reviews",
      "min": 3, "max": 12, "step": 1, "default": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "rotate_seconds",
      "label": "Auto-rotate every",
      "min": 0, "max": 20, "step": 1, "unit": "s", "default": 6,
      "info": "0 turns rotation off. It pauses while a shopper points at or tabs into the box, and never runs for shoppers whose device asks for reduced motion."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "lines",
      "label": "Lines of text before \"Read more\"",
      "min": 2, "max": 8, "step": 1, "default": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_stars",
      "label": "Show stars",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_verified",
      "label": "Show the Verified badge",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Only ever on reviews Marka Reviews matched to a real order."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_avatar",
      "label": "Show initial avatar",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Colours",
      "info": "Leave blank to follow the colours set in Marka Reviews → Settings → Display."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color",
      "label": "Border colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "Background colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "app_url",
      "label": "App URL",
      "default": "https://reviewmaster-app.azurewebsites.net",
      "info": "Leave as-is unless you run Marka Reviews on a custom domain."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
